# Lumen OS 1.0.4 (owner, 2026-10-15: "after restarting, adb over wifi is off"). LineageOS TV's "ADB over network"
# (Developer options) only sets the non-persistent service.adb.tcp.port (product init.lineage.atv.rc restarts adbd
# on 5555 / -1), so every reboot turned it off. Remember the user's own choice and restore it once the system is up.
# Nothing opens the port unless the user turned the switch on; adbd still runs only with USB debugging on and still
# asks for the computer's RSA key on screen (ro.adb.secure=1). Turning the switch off (-1) forgets it.
# 1.0.7: the restore runs ONCE per boot. In 1.0.4 to 1.0.6 it was triggered by persist.z9x.adb_net too, which the
# port rule below sets again (init fires on every set, also of the same value): restore -> port 5555 -> record ->
# restore ..., and init.lineage.atv.rc restarted adbd each time. A Z9X with USB debugging and ADB over network on
# had adbd killed every ~5 s for as long as it ran (no USB adb: sys.usb.ffs.ready=0, "udc failed to start g1: -19";
# no network adb either; owner's subscriber, 2026-10-28). Now the boot value is copied into sys.z9x.adb_net_boot
# once, and only that property restores the port.
on property:service.adb.tcp.port=5555
    setprop persist.z9x.adb_net 1

on property:service.adb.tcp.port=-1
    setprop persist.z9x.adb_net 0

on property:sys.boot_completed=1
    setprop sys.z9x.adb_net_boot ${persist.z9x.adb_net:-0}

on property:sys.z9x.adb_net_boot=1
    setprop service.adb.tcp.port 5555
